  "title": "Training datasets for epilepsy analysis: sliding-window features derived from the Freiburg intracranial EEG database (Riccio et al. 2024), processed-data release",
  "description": "This derivative dataset redistributes, unchanged, 20 per-patient feature tables derived from the Freiburg intracranial EEG database. Each row is a 2-s sliding window (1 s step) with 1080 univariate and bivariate features computed across six frequency bands for six electrodes (three in the epileptic focus, three outside it). Windows are labelled as pre-ictal, ictal, post-ictal or inter-ictal, for training machine-learning models for seizure analysis. No raw recordings are included.",
  "methods_description": "Intracranial EEG from six electrodes per patient (three focal, three non-focal; 256 Hz) was band-pass filtered into six bands (alpha to high gamma, 8-120 Hz). Fourteen univariate and eight bivariate features per electrode and band were computed in 2-s windows with a 1-s step, using the authors' Training Builder tool. Each window was labelled by seizure phase. The CSV files were copied byte-for-byte from the Zenodo record with md5 verification.",
